<title>USA: Leading lenders of U.S. commercial bank loans.</title>
<headline>Leading lenders of U.S. commercial bank loans.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Feb 5 (LPC) - The following table comprises leading issuers of commercial syndicated loans to U.S. borrowers, as compiled by Loan Pricing Corp.</p>
<p>Each lender with an agent or co-agent title on a deal</p>
<p>receives full credit for the transaction. Table is</p>
<p>year-to-date, ending February 5.</p>
<p>Rank Lender		Volume    # of	    Market</p>
<p>			     ($million) Deals	  Share(%)</p>
<p>1    BankAmerica	  $6,760     6		  16%</p>
<p>2    Chase Manhattan     3,895     5		   9</p>
<p>3    J.P. Morgan	   3,697     4		   9</p>
<p>4    ABN AMRO		2,590     5		   6</p>
<p>5    NationsBank	   2,565     7		   6</p>
<p>6    CS First Boston     1,975     3		   5</p>
<p>7    BankBoston	    1,850     2		   4</p>
<p>8    BZW/Barclays	  1,324     3		   3</p>
<p>9    Bank of New York    1,320     2		   3</p>
<p>10   Bankers Trust	 1,273     3		   3</p>
<p>11   CIBC Wood Gundy     1,075     2		   3</p>
<p>12   BNP		     1,000     1		   2</p>
<p>13   Fleet Financial	 994     3		   2</p>
<p>14   Bank of Montreal	900     1		   2</p>
<p>14   Sanwa Bank		900     1		   2</p>
<p>14   Toronto-Dominion	900     1		   2</p>
<p>14   Union Bank		900     1		   2</p>
<p>18   Goldman Sachs	   740     2		   2</p>
<p>18   Societe Generale	740     2		   2</p>
<p>20   Norwest Corporation   700     1		   2</p>
<p>20   Royal Bank of Canada  700     1		   2</p>
<p>((--Michele Walsh, LPC Editorial 212 499-5455))</p>
